          "recommended": false,
          "recommended_because": null,
          "text": "A dated commitment, a passed deadline and a published result. Almost nothing else we review has all three.\n\nMost bank climate commitments are restrictions with an effective date of “immediate” — rules about what will not be done, which can never be checked as met or missed. This one had a year on it, the year arrived, and the bank stated the outcome in a number. Watchtower records it as the only phase-out on the document.\n\nThe definition is also disclosed rather than assumed. Footnote 29 is on the same page as the commitment, and it says in plain terms what is excluded and why, including the PCAF Standard reference for guarantees. A bank trying to hide the shape of its measure does not print the measure.\n\nThe criticism belongs to what the measure leaves out and to the missing baseline — not to the existence of a dated target the bank then reported against."
