          "text": "Compare this to the coal commitments in the same review set and the difference is in kind, not in strength.\n\nSociété Générale promises to reduce thermal coal exposure to zero by 2030 in the EU and OECD and by 2040 everywhere else — dates far enough out that nobody currently in the room will be asked about them. SEB sets a 5% revenue threshold and applies it to whole business relationships, immediately, with no end date at all. Macquarie did something neither of them has done: it set a near date, reached it, and published the result.\n\nThe trade is visibility for scope. Société Générale's and SEB's commitments cover the client relationship; Macquarie's covers one accounting measure of one product line, with four categories subtracted. A checkable narrow promise and an uncheckable broad one are not comparable on a single scale, and pretending otherwise would flatter one of them.\n\nWhat would settle it is the 2021 baseline. Without it, the most checkable coal commitment in the set still cannot be checked."
